  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRCS/L Additional Response Preparedness</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">12 Palestinian refugee camps and nearby settlements (HQ Akka, North Area, South area, bekaa area, Beirut area)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities included in this project are: review / development of contigency plans; desk top simulations; advanced first aid training; emergency stock prepositioning; and equipping of volunteers</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of PRCS/L strategy action plan for 2022 to achieve Response an preparedness systems to be set, it is important to continue with the needed RP activities in order to have a prepared and trained teams in all areas to respond efficiently in crisis. This will complement contingency plans that where developed to test them and to make sure that all staff are fully aware of responsibilities during preparedness and response times. In addition, there will be in parallel procurement of emergency stock to equip the warehouses of hospitals in order to deliver medical services with good quality.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building and training is offered to staff personel of PRCS/L on HQ and branche level to assist Palestinian refugees in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRCS/L is providing secondary health services for Palestine and Syrian refugees, Lebanese and more. The project will aim to reduce the effect of the disaster when happened. Therefore this project will support PRCS/L to enhance its Response Preparedness capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
